message.content:
{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2176-08-02 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I’m Dr. Lee, one of your hospital doctors. You’re here for your 21st cycle of high-dose methotrexate, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2176-08-02 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I’ve been feeling okay since the last one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2176-08-02 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. Any headaches, vision changes, weakness, or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2176-08-02 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, nothing like that. Just my usual leg pain, but that’s been the same for years."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2176-08-02 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. We’ll keep an eye on that. Today, you’ll get IV fluids with bicarbonate to protect your kidneys and help clear the chemo. Then the methotrexate infusion later this afternoon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2176-08-02 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I’m getting fosaprepitant again instead of Zofran, right? I got bad headaches last time with Zofran."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2176-08-02 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. We’ve noted that. You’ll get fosaprepitant to prevent nausea, since Zofran didn’t agree with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2176-08-02 11:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. That makes me feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2176-08-02 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. The chemotherapy infusion started about 15 minutes ago. It’ll run for a few hours. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2176-08-02 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m okay so far. Just a little anxious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2176-08-02 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s understandable. You can take your lorazepam if you need it. We’re monitoring your urine pH to keep it above 8.5 — that helps the methotrexate clear safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2176-08-02 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. So the bicarbonate is doing that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2176-08-02 12:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. It keeps your urine alkaline, which protects your kidneys and helps flush the drug."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2176-08-03 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your methotrexate level came back this morning — it’s 0.13 micromolar at 36 hours, which is excellent. That means it’s clearing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2176-08-03 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2176-08-03 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Very good. We’ll start your leucovorin rescue soon — it helps protect your healthy cells from the chemo’s side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2176-08-03 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that from last time. But I did feel a bit nauseous yesterday evening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2176-08-03 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the nurse mentioned that. You took ativan and compazine, and it settled down?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2176-08-03 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, by this morning I felt fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2176-08-03 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Nausea can still happen even with good anti-nausea meds. We’ll keep those on hand just in case."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2176-08-03 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your brain MRI results are back. No signs of lymphoma recurrence — just stable changes from before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2176-08-03 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s such a relief. What about the sinus issue they mentioned?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2176-08-03 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "There’s some ongoing sinus inflammation, but it’s not new or serious. Nothing we need to treat now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2176-08-03 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. I’ve had sinus problems for years."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2176-08-03 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow morning. You’ll go home with three doses of leucovorin — one every six hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2176-08-03 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just three doses? Last time I took it longer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2176-08-03 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, because your methotrexate level dropped quickly, you only need one more day. That’s a sign your body cleared the drug well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2176-08-03 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds good. And I’ll keep taking my regular meds — gabapentin, citalopram, aspirin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2176-08-03 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, all your regular medications resume — including aspirin. We held it during admission for safety, but it’s fine to restart now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2176-08-03 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Because of the blood clot history?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2176-08-03 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We used heparin while you were here to prevent clots, and now aspirin will continue that protection at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2176-08-03 14:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my next chemo is in a month?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2176-08-03 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, cycle 22 is scheduled for next month. And you have a clinic visit soon for your Rituxan infusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2176-08-03 14:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, that’s part of the maintenance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2176-08-04 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I’ve reviewed everything — your labs, MRI, and how you’ve felt. You’re doing well and ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2176-08-04 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Just to confirm — I take the leucovorin every six hours, starting today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2176-08-04 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, four tablets each time — 40 mg total — three times. Then stop. And call if you develop unusual fatigue, mouth sores, or rash."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2176-08-04 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I feel nauseous again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2176-08-04 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You can use the prochlorperazine or lorazepam as needed. But it should get better now that the chemo is out of your system."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2176-08-04 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2176-08-04 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You did really well this cycle. Keep up with your appointments, and we’ll keep monitoring your progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2176-08-04 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. See you next month."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2176-08-04 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before discharge. Any new symptoms — pain, shortness of breath, swelling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2176-08-04 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, still feeling stable. My leg pain is the same, but it’s manageable with the oxycodone when needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2176-08-04 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. And your breathing? Any wheezing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2176-08-04 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, asthma’s been quiet. I’ve been using my inhaler as usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2176-08-04 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. I’ll sign the discharge orders. The nurse will go over your prescriptions and instructions one more time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2176-08-04 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2176-08-04 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing — your depression meds. Are you still seeing your counselor?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2176-08-04 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, every other week. Citalopram helps, but the counseling makes a big difference."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2176-08-04 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. Keep that up. Mental health is just as important as physical health, especially during treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2176-08-04 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I agree. It’s been a long journey, but I’m managing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2176-08-04 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing an excellent job. We’ll see you soon for the next cycle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2176-08-04 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Looking forward to it. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2176-08-04 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final check — all labs stable, no signs of infection or bleeding, neuro exam normal. You’re cleared to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2176-08-04 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. I’m ready to get back to my routine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2176-08-04 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take it easy for a few days. Rest, stay hydrated, and follow up as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2176-08-04 12:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2176-08-04 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2176-08-04 12:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. See you next time."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2176-08-02 10:42:00",
    "admission_end": "2176-08-04 13:05:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 50-year-old woman with primary central nervous system lymphoma was admitted for her 21st cycle of high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy. She reported feeling well with no neurological or systemic symptoms. The chemotherapy was administered safely with urine alkalinization maintained throughout. She received fosaprepitant for nausea prophylaxis due to prior headaches with Zofran, and experienced mild nausea on day two, which resolved with ativan and compazine. Her methotrexate level at 36 hours was 0.13 micromolar, indicating safe clearance. A brain MRI showed no evidence of lymphoma recurrence, with only stable chronic changes. She remained neurologically and hematologically stable. Aspirin was held during admission and restarted at discharge, with heparin bridging for DVT prophylaxis. She was discharged home in stable condition with a short course of oral leucovorin and instructions to continue her regular medications for chronic pain, asthma, and depression.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Primary central nervous system lymphoma, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Pain in limb",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Personal history of pulmonary embolism",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
